== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

=== Composite Phases as Master Equation Term Implementations ===

The three composite phases implement three distinct terms in the master equation. Within the ψ hypothesis (Track B), each phase has a specific psionic function beyond its electromagnetic role:

'''BST phase — αF²μν coupling control:''' The voltage-tunable <math>\varepsilon_{\rm eff}(V)</math> modulates the effective coupling coefficient <math>\alpha_{\rm eff}</math> between the bifilar coil EM field and the ψ source term. High-bias (200V) operation reduces <math>\varepsilon_{\rm eff}</math>, which shifts the impedance <math>Z_\psi = (1/\omega^2)\sqrt{\mu_\psi/\varepsilon_\psi}</math> (from [[ψ Impedance Theory]] A4), enabling real-time impedance matching adjustment without mechanical reconfiguration.

'''PZT-5H phase — −λψ³ soliton support:''' The parametric amplification provided by the piezoelectric matrix at Shepard tone acoustic frequencies (10, 20, 40 kHz) feeds energy into the ψ field amplitude at precisely the frequencies where the <math>-\lambda\psi^3</math> nonlinear term would otherwise cause soliton amplitude decay. The PZT response compensates the nonlinear damping, sustaining the soliton envelope that provides the stable reference state during Anchor mode.

'''Ferrofluid phase — −m²ψ coherence length control:''' The H-field-tunable <math>\mu_{\rm eff}(H)</math> of the ferrofluid channels sets <math>m_{\rm eff}</math> and therefore <math>L_\psi = 1/m_{\rm eff}</math> in real time. This is the only independently controllable parameter that can shift the coherence length during operation without changing drive frequency or cavity geometry. The [[Anchor Controller]] (D6) uses this as its primary mechanism for adapting the device to the operator's current effective mass (which shifts with ψ₀ background from the [[ψ Dispersion Relations]] A3 nonlinear mass formula).

== TML Measurement Protocol ==

=== TML-1 — Bench Characterisation (No Subjects) ===

Fabricate three tablet samples (10 mm diameter, 2 mm thick) per batch following the full protocol above. Measure:

# <math>\varepsilon_{\rm eff}(V)</math> curve from 0 to 200V DC bias at 40 kHz using Keysight E4990A impedance analyser + 42841A bias adapter.
# <math>\tan\delta</math> at 40 kHz, 0V bias.
# <math>d_{33,\rm eff}</math> using Berlincourt piezometer (APC International Model 8000).
# Ferrofluid <math>M(H)</math> curve using vibrating sample magnetometer (VSM; Lakeshore 7400 or equivalent) on extracted channel ferrofluid sample.
# DC surface resistance using Keithley 6517B electrometer.

'''Pass criteria:'''
* <math>\varepsilon_{\rm eff}</math> tunability <math>\geq 0.08</math>
* <math>\tan\delta < 0.01</math> at 40 kHz
* <math>d_{33,\rm eff} > 40</math> pC/N
* <math>M_{\rm sat}</math> within 10% of EMG-900 spec sheet value
* Surface resistance > 10 MΩ

=== TML-2 — Integrated Shell Test (No Subjects) ===

Integrate full composite-filled shell with bifilar coil drive. Measure:

# <math>\varepsilon_{\rm eff}</math> uniformity across shell surface: VNA S-parameter map at 5 cm spatial resolution. Target: < 15% variation shell-to-shell and position-to-position.
# Thermal stability: cycle shell through 15–40°C (simulated HelmKit operating range). Confirm <math>\varepsilon_{\rm eff}</math> drift < 5%.
# Ferrofluid <math>\mu_{\rm eff}(H)</math> response in-situ: vary control coil current; measure inductive response of drive coil. Confirm Langevin model matches within 20%.

